From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] grt: an edge used past 100x its capacity is a warning

A grt bug: check2DEdgesUsage stops global route when one gcell edge
carries more than 100 times the per-edge capacity, also when the route
was asked to accept congestion (-allow_congestion), which the end of
routing honours (GRT-0115 warning, GRT-0116 error otherwise).

On XiangShan's XSTile parent, CTS latency balancing inserts 2,502 delay
buffers, 290 of them within 11 um of the root of the 151k-sink register
clock tree; about 3,900 route segments cross single gcell edges there
against the 3,900 limit (39 tracks), and the parent's global route
(-congestion_iterations 0 -allow_congestion) stops before it writes a
routed database. As a warning the route completes, with 54 edges over
the limit, all in that box.

A temporary unblock, warning unconditionally: the flow passes
-allow_congestion here. The fix is upstream as
The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD#11754 (it keeps the early error without
-allow_congestion); this patch is dropped at the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD that carries it.

---
diff --git a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/utility.cpp b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/utility.cpp
index aeab6d4d40..e5744b5496 100644
--- a/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/utility.cpp
+++ b/src/grt/src/fastroute/src/utility.cpp
@@ -2023,7 +2023,7 @@ void FastRouteCore::check2DEdgesUsage()
   // check horizontal edges
   for (const auto& [x, y] : graph2d_.getUsedGridsH()) {
     if (graph2d_.getUsageH(x, y) > max_h_edge_usage) {
-      logger_->error(GRT,
+      logger_->warn(GRT,
                      228,
                      "Horizontal edge usage exceeds the maximum allowed. "
                      "({}, {}) usage={} limit={}",
@@ -2037,7 +2037,7 @@ void FastRouteCore::check2DEdgesUsage()
   // check vertical edges
   for (const auto& [x, y] : graph2d_.getUsedGridsV()) {
     if (graph2d_.getUsageV(x, y) > max_v_edge_usage) {
-      logger_->error(GRT,
+      logger_->warn(GRT,
                      229,
                      "Vertical edge usage exceeds the maximum allowed. "
                      "({}, {}) usage={} limit={}",
